id: pm-native-git-retry-proof
title: Prove native Git lock retry after observed contention in PR1425
description: "CodeRabbit PR1425 identified that a fixed 200ms fixture release can precede the first configuration write, allowing the native Git retry regression to pass without contention. Preserve the closed production-fix owner and strengthen acceptance with observed genuine Git failure, deterministic owner release and a disabled-retry negative control."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-07T20:10:22.629Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-07T20:16:33.822Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-07T20:16:00.113Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-07T20:16:00.113Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Native Git must first return its genuine lock-exists failure before the fixture writer releases its owned lock; the installation then retries successfully. Disabling retry makes this regression fail. All-platform concurrent and unchanged-config checks remain separate and pass.
parent: pm-gh1424
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Replace timer-only contention proof with an executable proxy that preserves native Git commands, output and status; release the fixture-owned lock only after the genuine lock-exists error. Share native instrumentation with the malformed-config race and keep concurrent/idempotent checks on all platforms."
expected_result: The retry regression requires observed external contention and fails when retry is disabled; concurrent setup and unchanged configuration stay covered.
actual_result: "Both linked suites passed all 28 cases. A temporary disabled-retry negative control failed with the genuine configuration refusal and original source was restored. Typechecking, ESLint and zero-duplication checks passed. The proxy cases are Unix-only; real all-platform configuration tests remain enabled."
